UPDATE companies SET description='EightTwenty is based in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. The company was founded in 2020 by Tony Capucille, who previously served as president of Heartland Payment Systems, and Kent Cissell, a former senior vice president at Global Payments, joined as co‑founder and president. The business is employee‑owned with local investors in each market it serves, a structure intended to align the company’s interests with the communities where it operates. Capucille established EightTwenty after two decades in the payments industry, driven by a desire to address the country’s energy challenges through solar power.

The firm designs and installs solar photovoltaic systems for residential, commercial, and tax‑exempt customers, integrating battery storage and EV charging where needed. Its in‑house craftsmen handle installation and commissioning, and the company operates across Oklahoma, Texas, Arkansas, Indiana, and Kentucky. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

EightTwenty serves homeowners, businesses, non‑profits, and builder partners. Concrete examples from its testimonials include a brewery owner who values producing electricity alongside beer and a developer of the Kindred Spirits community. The company also runs a “Give Solar” program that directs a portion of each sale to fund solar installations for neighbors who cannot afford them.

Capucille founded EightTwenty to bring clean, renewable energy to Middle America, a region he saw as under‑served despite strong solar potential. The company emphasizes a culture built on respect, focus, and quality, aiming to turn every customer into a “raving fan” and to elevate the solar industry’s standards in the region.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design", "Solar installation", "Solar storage integration", "EV charging integration", "Commercial solar development", "Residential solar installation", "Non-profit solar development", "Builder partnership programs"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Non-profit", "Builder/Developer"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned with local investors in each market", "In-house installation craftsmen", "Give Solar program funds solar for neighbors", "Vertically integrated solar developer focused on Middle America"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 by Tony Capucille -> db", "Headquarters Oklahoma City, Oklahoma -> db", "Employee-owned with local investors -> /about-us", "In-house installation craftsmen -> /", "Give Solar program -> /", "Serves Oklahoma, Texas, Arkansas, Indiana, Kentucky -> /about-us", "Founders: Tony Capucille, Kent Cissell -> /about-us", "Company type: installer/service -> /", "Vertically integrated solar developer -> /about-us", "Culture of respect, focus, quality -> /about-us", "Testimonials from brewery owner and developer -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We started with the plan to build a vertically integrated solar developer to serve Middle America.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/eighttwentyenergy/"], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHE