is located in the Minneapolis/Saint Paul, Minnesota area with a 75,000 square foot manufacturing facility", "founded_year": "1957", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electric-wire-products-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Equipment LLC has operated from Idaho Falls, Idaho since 1962. The company is owned and led by Brook Jensen, a Licensed Master Electrician with over 30 years of hands-on experience. Jensen founded the business and serves as president, overseeing estimating, project management, safety compliance, and customer relationships. The firm has built a reputation across Eastern Idaho for reliable electrical work backed by a master electrician on every job.

The company provides full-spectrum electrical services through six divisions: residential (panel upgrades, new circuits, EV charger installations, safety inspections), commercial (preventive maintenance, LED retrofits, lighting controls, tenant improvements, code compliance), industrial (three-phase power distribution, motor controls and VFDs, motor control centers, switchgear maintenance, conduit systems, outage coordination), agricultural (irrigation pump wiring, grain bin systems, barn wiring, livestock facility power, weatherproof installations), generators and emergency power (generator connections, transfer switches, UPS coordination, standby power testing), and government/institutional work (SAM.gov registered, OSHA and NFPA 70E compliant, written lockout/tagout program, full documentation). A crew of eight licensed electricians, including foreman Ken Cathey with 30-plus years of experience, executes projects within a 200-mile radius of Idaho Falls.

The company''s SAM.gov registration and compliance with federal work-authorization requirements enable it to serve institutional clients directly.

Electrical Equipment LLC emphasizes integrity, safety, and documentation. Every job follows a mandatory test-before-touch protocol, arc-flash PPE requirements, and a written lockout/tagout program aligned with NFPA 70E. The firm commits to a two-hour emergency response for critical outages, provides before-and-after photos with test readings and written completion reports, and carries $1 million in general liability insurance and $1 million in bonding. All projects are managed through professional software for real-time scheduling, digital invoicing, and complete job history.', certifications=ARRAY['OSHA 10','OSHA 30','NFPA 70E','SAM.gov registered (UEI: DZU2WXSS6K6)','Idaho Master Electrician License #052024','Idaho Electrical Contractor License #056784','$1M General Liability Insurance','$1M Bonding']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential electrical services (panel upgrades, new circuits, GFCI/AFCI protection, EV charger installation, home safety inspections, ceiling fan and lighting installation)", "Commercial electrical maintenance and installation (preventive maintenance programs, LED lighting retrofits, lighting controls and sensors, tenant improvement wiring, emergency and exit lighting, code compliance upgrades)", "Industrial electrical systems (three-phase power distribution, motor controls and VFDs, motor control centers (MCCs), switchgear and panel maintenance, conduit systems, planned outage coordination)", "Agricultural electrical systems (irrigation pump wiring, grain bin and elevator systems, barn and outbuilding wiring, livestock facility power, weatherproof installations, load management systems)", "Generator and emergency power systems (generator connections and hookup, automatic transfer switches, manual transfer switches, UPS system coordination, emergency lighting systems, standby power testing)", "Government and institutional electrical services (SAM.gov registered, OSHA and NFPA 70E compliance, written LOTO safety program, full documentation and reporting, work authorization compliance)", "2-hour emergency response for critical outages"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Government", "Institutional"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["2-hour emergency response for critical outages and safety hazards", "SAM.gov registered (UEI: DZU2WXSS6K6) with federal work-authorization compliance", "OSHA and NFPA 70E compliant with written lockout/tagout program and mandatory test-before-touch protocol", "Master Electrician on every job; $1M general liability insurance and $1M bonding", "Documented work with before/after photos, test readings, and written completion reports"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1962 in Idaho Falls, Idaho -> db and homepage", "Owned and led by Brook Jensen, Licensed Master Electrician -> homepage and team page", "8 licensed electricians on staff -> homepage", "Services: residential, commercial, industrial, agricultural, generators, government -> homepage", "SAM.gov registered (UEI: DZU2WXSS6K6) -> homepage", "OSHA & NFPA 70E compliant with written LOTO program -> homepage", "2-hour emergency response commitment -> homepage", "$1M general liability insurance and $1M bonding -> homepage", "Master Electrician license #052024, ID License #056784 -> homepage", "Foreman Ken Cathey with 30+ years experience -> homepage", "Serves Eastern Idaho within 200-mile radius -> homepage", "Professional job management software for scheduling, invoicing, job history -> homepage"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Licensed electrical contractors serving residential, commercial, industrial, and agricultural customers across Eastern Idaho.", "founded_year": "1962", "employee_count": "8 licensed electricians", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now()