UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Design & Research Inc. (EDR) operates from Louisville, Kentucky, under the holding company VSHolding LLC. The business was founded by Vladimir A. Shvartsman, Ph.D., who remains the principal figure behind its engineering focus.

The product range extends to full-bridge drivers for piezo transducers and DC motors, DC/DC converters, active and powerline notch filters for medical signal acquisition, ultra-fast I-V bias generators for MRI spectroscopy, and the Super High-Power Switching Apparatus (SHPSA) that delivers up to 1.6 MW pulses from a 19-inch rack cabinet. The company also produces the UPEL-2500 bench-top electronic load system for testing power sources up to 100 kHz, and offers custom development with no engineering fee plus repair services.

The company serves OEM medical device makers building cardio stimulators and high-resolution electrocardiographs, automotive suppliers for cars, motorcycles, and forklifts, defense contractors, and industrial automation users such as robot and X-Y table builders. Power-test laboratories like MET Laboratories have procured SHPSA units for high-current testing, while telecommunications and UPS manufacturers use the electronic loads for qualification.

