UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Polymer Technologies was founded in 2006 in Chandler, Arizona. The company specializes in NASA-grade conformal coating services for electronic components and circuit boards.

The company provides conformal coating, potting, encapsulation, component staking and bonding, BGA rework, SMT assembly, and mechanical assembly services. Processes include spraying, dipping, brushing, and selective coating systems with advanced masking techniques. Facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

The company serves aerospace, military, automotive, consumer goods, and medical device industries.

Electronic Polymer Technologies emphasizes its AS9100 and ITAR compliance, over 20 years of experience with IPC A-610 standards, fast turnaround times, and customized coating solutions using materials such as parylene, acrylic, epoxy, polyurethane, and silicone.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Conformal coating (spray, dip, brush, selective coating)", "Circuit board potting", "Component encapsulation", "Component staking and bonding", "BGA rework and re-balling", "SMT assembly (fine pitch, ultra fine pitch, PBGA, CBGA, micro BGA)", "Mechanical assembly", "CPC4 repair", "Connector installation", "Jumper and wiring installation", "Plated through-hole installation", "Advanced masking techniques", "Custom coating material selection", "IPC A-610 quality inspection", "Fast turnaround services"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Military", "Automotive", "Consumer goods", "Medical devices"], "materials": ["Parylene", "Acrylic", "Epoxy", "Polyurethane", "Silicone"], "equipment": ["Selective coating systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NASA-grade conformal coating services", "AS9100 and ITAR certified", "Over 20 years of IPC A-610 and conformal coating experience", "Fast turnaround with advanced selective coating systems", "Customized coating solutions for extreme temperature and chemical resistance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2006 in Chandler, Arizona -> db", "NASA-grade conformal coating services -> /", "AS9100 and ITAR certifications -> db, /", "Over 20 years experience in IPC A-610 and conformal coating -> /", "Services: conformal coating, potting, encapsulation, staking, bonding, BGA rework, SMT, mechanical assembly -> /services", "Processes: spray, dip, brush, selective coating, advanced masking -> /", "Industries: aerospace, military, automotive, consumer goods, medical devices -> /, /about", "Materials: parylene, acrylic, epoxy, polyurethane, silicone -> /", "Fast turnaround, customized solutions -> /, /services", "Headquarters Chandler, Arizona -> db, /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Electronic Polymer Technologies is a NASA Grade conformal coating business that services all countries.", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electronic-polymer-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Services Inc. is a family-owned and operated communications company based in Winfield, West Virginia. It traces its roots to 1971 when it began serving first responders, government agencies, school systems, businesses, and the general public across the state. The company was incorporated in October 1988. In the spring of 1997, it built its first full-service sales, service, and installation facility in Winfield, where it remains today. In 2021, the company completed a new 5,000-square-foot state-of-the-art vehicle upfitters installation facility to expand its capacity.

The company provides a range of communication products and services. Its product lines include emergency lighting, vehicle consoles, dispatch consoles, law enforcement radar, paging systems, vehicle safety products, and car audio. It also installs video surveillance security systems, burglar alarms, and mobile and home audio/video systems. Services cover radio system design, configuration, programming, installation, deployment, training, ongoing support, radio servicing and repair, radio rentals, mobile installations, vehicle buildouts, and field and mountaintop service response throughout West Virginia. The combined staff experience totals 70 years.

Electronic Services Inc. serves public safety agencies (law enforcement, fire, EMS), government entities, school systems, commercial businesses, and the general public. Concrete examples include designing and installing 911 communication consoles for counties, equipping vehicles for first responders, and providing two-way radios for recreational use such as hunting trips. The company also works with automotive aftermarket brands such as Westin Automotive for vehicle safety products.

The company emphasizes quality installations, stating it takes no shortcuts and uses only the highest-quality tools, products, and procedures with a goal of 100 percent correctness. It was founded to serve first responders—referred to as ''local heroes''—and aims to expand that mission with its expanded upfitting facility.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Radio system design", "Radio configuration and programming", "Radio installation and deployment", "Radio training and support", "Radio servicing and repair", "Radio rentals", "Mobile radio installations", "Vehicle buildouts and upfitting", "Field and mountaintop service response", "Video surveillance system installation", "Burglar alarm installation", "Mobile and home A/V system installation", "Emergency lighting installation", "Vehicle console installation", "Dispatch console installation", "Law enforcement radar installation", "Paging system installation", "Vehicle safety product installation", "Car audio installation", "Consultations"], "industries": ["Public safety", "Government", "Education", "Commercial", "General public", "Automotive aftermarket"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1971", "5,000 sq ft vehicle upfitting facility completed in 2021", "Field and mountaintop service response across West Virginia", "Combined 70 years of industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 -> db", "Incorporated October 1988 -> /about", "First facility built 1997 in Winfield, WV -> /about", "New 5,000 sq ft upfitting facility completed 2021 -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> db", "Kenwood dealer since late 1980s -> /about", "Combined 70 years experience -> /about", "Services: radio system design, installation, repair, rentals, mobile installations, vehicle buildouts, field service -> /services", "Products: two-way radios, emergency lighting, vehicle consoles, dispatch consoles, law enforcement radar, paging, vehicle safety products, car audio, video surveillance, burglar alarms, mobile/home A/V -> /about, /", "Industries served: first responders, government agencies, school systems, businesses, general public -> db", "Headquarters: Winfield, West Virginia -> db", "Company type: installer/service company -> /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are experts at designing and building complete radio systems from the ground up, or fixing your existing communications system.", "founded_year": "1971", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electronic-service-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Solutions Inc (ESI) operates from St. Louis, Missouri, as a division of Indak. The company traces its roots back more than two decades, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. It began with a focus on quality, service, and price, positioning itself as an automotive electronics solutions provider.

ESI functions as a full-service electronic and electro-mechanical contract manufacturer. Its capabilities span complex PCB assembly, electro-mechanical assembly, circuit assembly, wire harness fabrication, and complete box-build systems that integrate enclosures, power supplies, cables, and PCB assemblies with system configuration programming, functional test, and burn-in. The company manages the supply chain for components and supports projects from prototype through mass production, offering design services, test apparatus development, project management, and supply chain management.

The customer base includes automotive suppliers, appliance manufacturers, commercial equipment makers, medical device companies, and commercial printing firms. ESI provides dedicated product teams for each customer to manage component sourcing and final assembly.

