UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Hazelwood, Missouri, Elite Printing and Packaging is a family-owned business that operates as a single-source partner for custom printing, packaging, co-packing, and fulfillment. The company serves brands across the St. Louis region and beyond from its facility in the St. Louis metro area.

Elite produces flexible packaging using digital and rotogravure presses, creating rollstock, labels, shrink sleeves, tamper bands, retail cartons, and point-of-sale materials. Its packaging line includes stand-up, gusseted, and flat pouches, pillow packs, sachets, jars, tubes, and canisters, with eco-friendly options such as recyclable, compostable, matte, and metallic finishes. Co-packing capabilities cover vertical form-fill-seal (VFFS) pouching for treats, snacks, and powders, flow-wrapped pillow packs, jar and tube filling, and kitting, labeling, and assembly. Fulfillment services span e-commerce and retail order processing, pick-and-pack, POS assembly, lot tracking, inventory management, and LTL/FTL shipping with daily UPS and FedEx pickups. The company handles runs from small batches to high-volume production.

Elite''s customer base centers on the food sector, particularly pet food and human food brands. The company cites experience with pet treats, snacks, powders, and specialty food products, and works with brands launching new items, preparing for retail distribution, or seeking to streamline their supply chain.

The company emphasizes its all-in-one model, traceable lot control with quality assurance at every step, fast turnaround times, flexible order minimums, and a family-owned, detail-driven culture as its primary differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Flexible packaging film printing", "Label printing", "Shrink sleeve printing", "Tamper band printing", "Retail carton & display printing", "Digital printing", "Rotogravure printing", "Stand-up pouch manufacturing", "Gusseted pouch manufacturing", "Flat pouch manufacturing", "Pillow pack manufacturing", "Sachet manufacturing", "Jar/tube/canister packaging", "Eco-friendly packaging options (recyclable, compostable, matte, metallic)", "Vertical form fill seal (VFFS) pouching", "Flow wrapping & pillow packs", "Powder filling", "Jar, tube, & bottle filling", "Kitting & assembly", "Stand-up pouch/carousel filling", "E-commerce fulfillment", "Pick & pack services", "POS assembly", "Shipping & distribution (LTL/FTL, UPS/FedEx)"], "industries": ["Pet food", "Human food", "Snacks", "Treats", "Powders", "Specialty food products"], "materials": ["Flexible packaging films", "Labels", "Shrink sleeves", "Tamper bands", "Cartons", "Stand-up pouches", "Gusseted pouches", "Flat pouches", "Pillow packs", "Sachets", "Jars", "Tubes", "Canisters", "Recyclable materials", "Compostable materials", "Matte finishes", "Metallic finishes"], "equipment": ["Stand Up Pouch/Carousel Filling Machine"], "volume": "Small to high-volume runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All-in-one printing, packaging, co-packing & fulfillment", "Traceable lot control and QA built into every step", "Fast turnaround & flexible order minimums", "Experienced with pet & human food products", "Family-owned, detail-driven, and focused on your success"], "facts_used": ["Hazelwood, Missouri headquarters -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "All-in-one printing, packaging, co-packing & fulfillment -> /", "Traceable lot control and QA built into every step -> /", "Fast turnaround & flexible order minimums -> /", "Experienced with pet & human food products -> /", "Digital & rotogravure printing -> /", "VFFS pouching for treats, snacks, powders -> /", "Flow-wrapped pillow packs -> /", "Jar & tube filling -> /", "Kitting, labeling, & assembly -> /", "Pick & Pack, POS assembly, and kitting -> /", "Lot tracking & inventory management -> /", "LTL / FTL shipping, UPS / FedEx daily pickups -> /", "Stand Up Pouch/Carousel Filling Machine -> /", "Eco-friendly options (recyclable, compostable, matte, metallic) -> /", "Small to high-volume runs -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Your packaging comes to life on our presses.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/elite-printing-and-packaging/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='elite-printing-and-packaging-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Elite Spice Inc., founded in 1988, is a privately-held, American-owned spice importer and custom manufacturer headquartered in Sparks, Nevada. The company operates six facilities across the East and West coasts, with a focus on food safety and purity.

The company supplies an extensive line of spices, herbs, seasonings, capsicums, onion and garlic, dehydrated fruits and vegetables, and specialty food ingredients. Its manufacturing operations include cleaning, milling, custom blending, packaging, and validated microbial reduction and pathogen elimination systems, all controlled in-house. A culinary innovation center and multiple R&D laboratories support product development.

Elite Spice serves all segments of the commercial food industry, providing ingredients for some of the world’s most popular food brands. Its customer base includes food manufacturers and processors seeking custom blends and technical support.

The company differentiates itself through its “Processed in the USA” commitment, maintaining direct control over the entire manufacturing process from raw material sourcing to finished goods. Its quality assurance laboratories conduct a wide range of tests to ensure compliance with U.S. federal regulations and food safety laws.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Spice Importing", "Custom Blending", "Milling", "Cleaning", "Microbial Reduction", "Pathogen Elimination", "Packaging", "Research & Development", "Technical Services", "Sales Support", "Quality Control", "Food Safety Testing"], "industries": ["Commercial Food Industry", "Food Manufacturing", "Food Processing", "Food Ingredients"], "materials": ["Spices", "Herbs", "Seasonings", "Capsicums", "Onion", "Garlic", "Dehydrated Fruits", "Dehydrated Vegetables", "Specialty Food Ingredients"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 -> db", "Headquarters in Sparks, Nevada -> db", "14 employees -> db", "Six facilities on East and West coasts -> /about", "Privately-held American ownership -> /about", "Spice importer and custom manufacturer -> /", "Processes: cleaning, milling, blending, packaging -> /about", "Microbial reduction and pathogen elimination -> /about", "Culinary innovation center and R&D labs -> /about", "Serves commercial food industry -> /about", "Quality assurance labs -> /quality", "Compliance with US Federal regulations -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "is an industry leading spice importer and custom manufacturer offering an extensive line of spices, seasonings and specialty food ingredients.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "14", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='elite-spice-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ellerbuilt Woodworks operates from Carson City, Nevada, where founder Brandon Eller established the shop as an expression of a lifelong dedication to woodworking. Eller traces his craft to childhood experiences — fixing and refinishing pieces by age ten — and a deep admiration for Japanese joinery traditions. The business remains owner‑operated, with Eller personally overseeing design, construction, and finishing of every commission.

The company produces custom cabinetry and handcrafted furniture for residential spaces. Its portfolio spans kitchen and bathroom cabinets, built‑ins, shelving, wall units, media cabinets, home‑office furniture (including partner and standing desks), bedroom pieces such as headboards, dressers, and bunk beds, as well as kitchen islands, custom pantries, eat‑in tables, bar cabinets, and home‑theater millwork. Work combines traditional hand‑tool joinery with modern machining and finishing techniques, using conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, and UV‑cured finishes. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

Projects are typically commissioned for kitchens, baths, home offices, bedrooms, and entertainment areas. The shop works with a broad palette of domestic and exotic hardwoods — oak, maple, cherry, walnut, redwood, cedar, and other specialty species — selected during a consultation process that matches material to the project’s aesthetic and durability requirements.

Eller positions the business on an uncompromising standard of craftsmanship: each piece is built to heirloom quality, with meticulous attention to detail and a deliberate, patient process. The founder’s philosophy — "if something is easy to do, it’s not worth doing" — drives a practice that favors the more difficult path when it yields a better result, aiming to create objects that endure across generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinet making", "Handcrafted furniture construction", "Built\u2011in cabinetry and shelving", "Wood joinery (traditional and modern methods)", "Wood finishing (conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, UV\u2011cured finish)", "Design consultation and material selection", "Custom millwork for kitchens, baths, offices, bedrooms, and entertainment spaces"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Interior design", "Custom furniture manufacturing", "Cabinetry", "Architectural millwork"], "materials": ["Oak", "Maple", "Cherry", "Walnut", "Redwood", "Cedar", "Exotic hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Few weeks for small projects, several months for large projects", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Owner\u2011operated by a single craftsman who personally designs and builds every piece", "Blend of traditional hand\u2011tool joinery with modern machining and finishing", "Wide selection of domestic and exotic hardwoods chosen per project", "Finishes include conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, and UV\u2011cured coatings", "No\u2011compromise approach: each piece inspected throughout for durability and aesthetics"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Carson City, Nevada -> db", "Founder: Brandon Eller -> page /", "Business description: custom cabinets and handcrafted furniture -> page /", "Product categories: kitchen cabinets, bathroom cabinets, built\u2011ins, shelves, wall units, media cabinets, office furniture, desks, bedroom furniture, kitchen islands, pantries, eat\u2011in tables, bar cabinets, home theater -> page /", "Processes: traditional joinery, modern techniques, finishes (conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, UV\u2011cured) -> page /", "Materials: oak, maple, cherry, walnut, redwood, cedar, exotic hardwoods -> page /", "Lead time: few weeks for small projects, several months for large projects -> page /", "Philosophy: no compromises, heirloom quality, deliberate process -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Cabinets & Handcrafted Furniture | Ellerbuilt Woodworks", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ellerbuilt-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ellis Fabrics operates in Bentonville, Arkansas, as the retail arm of Joe Ellis Upholstery. Joe Ellis began upholstering in 2002, working with independent shops across Arkansas and Louisiana. He opened Joe Ellis Upholstery in 2008, and the business grew to a larger space within five years. In 2013, Ellis and his mother, Cheryl, added a fabric store to answer customers'' frequent question about where to buy materials.

The business runs two workrooms staffed by nine full-time professionals and additional part-time help. They produce custom upholstery for residential, commercial, and specialty projects, handling everything from frame repair to final fabric application. The fabric store stocks a wide range of upholstery and home décor fabrics, trims, designer lines, real and faux leather, and outdoor and specialty materials, with special-order capability. A designer is on site to assist with selection and durability questions.

Clients span residential homeowners, hospitality venues (restaurants, bars, hotels, museums), medical and fitness facilities, and RV/motorhome owners. Notable customers include the Roark Group (design and fabrication), Onyx Coffee Lab (hospitality), Laura''s Draperies & Blinds (window treatments), and various interior designers across Arkansas, Oklahoma, and Missouri.

The company emphasizes a full-service experience from consultation through delivery, offering pick-up and delivery and promoting the motto "If you can dream it, we can upholster it." Their differentiation rests on in-house design guidance, a broad fabric inventory, and the ability to handle unique, tight-timeline projects.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom upholstery fabrication", "Residential upholstery", "Commercial upholstery (restaurant, bar, hotel, museum)", "Medical & fitness equipment upholstery", "RV/motorhome/outdoor furniture upholstery", "Antique furniture restoration", "Cushion fabrication", "Fabric retail (upholstery, home d\u00e9cor, trims)", "Designer fabric special orders", "Leather upholstery (real and faux)", "Outdoor and specialty fabric application", "Design consultation", "Pick-up and delivery service"], "industries": ["Residential", "Hospitality (restaurant, bar, hotel, museum)", "Medical & fitness", "RV/motorhome/outdoor", "Custom/one-of-a-kind"], "materials": ["Upholstery fabrics", "Home d\u00e9cor fabrics", "Trims", "Designer fabrics", "Real leather", "Faux leather", "Outdoor fabrics", "Specialty fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First-rate customer service since 2008", "Full-service experience from consultation to finished piece", "Pick-up and delivery available", "On-site designer for fabric selection and durability advice", "Special-order designer fabrics, real and faux leather, outdoor and specialty fabrics"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bentonville, Arkansas -> /", "Founded 2008 -> /about-us", "Founder Joe Ellis started upholstering in 2002 -> /about-us", "Mother Cheryl added fabric store in 2013 -> /about-us", "9 full-time professionals, two workrooms -> /about-us", "Services: custom upholstery, fabric retail, design consultation, pick up/delivery -> /, /about-us", "Industries served: residential, hospitality, medical & fitness, RV/motorhome/outdo