UPDATE companies SET description='Emergent Solar Energy is headquartered in West Lafayette, Indiana, within the Purdue Research Park. The leadership team includes Jeremy Lipinski, Adam Bolen, and Zacaria Martinez.

The firm operates as a full-service solar EPC contractor, delivering turnkey solar photovoltaic and battery energy storage systems under a single contract. Its integrated delivery model covers feasibility analysis, site-specific engineering with performance modeling, equipment procurement, construction management, utility interconnection, and commissioning. The company reports over 10 years of commercial and industrial project experience, with a documented 99.89% operational uptime across active facilities.

Emergent serves manufacturing, agricultural, municipal, institutional, and commercial clients throughout Indiana and neighboring states. Notable projects include a solar installation for Subaru of Indiana Automotive. The company focuses on facilities with complex energy loads, offering solutions that reduce operating costs, manage demand charges, and support sustainability goals.

The company emphasizes disciplined engineering, construction quality, and long-term asset performance. Its differentiation includes PE-engineered designs, component selection driven by warranty strength and supply-chain reliability, and a 25-year production warranty backed by a 5-year workmanship guarantee. The mission centers on fortifying Indiana businesses through energy independence and cost reduction.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Feasibility & Site Analysis", "Design & System Engineering", "Procurement & Construction", "Interconnection & Commissioning", "Solar Project Financing & Incentives", "Commercial & Industrial Solar EPC", "Agricultural Solar EPC", "Municipal & Institutional Solar EPC", "Commercial Battery Energy Storage Systems", "System Performance Monitoring", "Ongoing Service & Support"], "industries": ["Manufacturing", "Agriculture", "Municipal", "Institutional", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Solar PV modules (Tier-1)", "Inverters", "Battery energy storage systems", "Balance-of-system components"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Ranked #1 Commercial-Industrial Solar EPC in Indiana by Solar Power World", "Turnkey EPC delivery under a single contract (engineering, procurement, construction, interconnection, commissioning)", "PE-engineered designs with pre-procurement performance modeling", "25-year production warranty and 5-year workmanship guarantee", "99.89% proven operational system uptime across 100% active commercial/industrial facilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in West Lafayette, Indiana (Purdue Research Park) -> /", "Founded in 2014 -> /about-us", "Founders/management: Jeremy Lipinski, Adam Bolen, Zacaria Martinez -> /about-us", "Full-service solar EPC contractor delivering turnkey solar PV and battery energy storage systems -> /", "Integrated delivery: feasibility, design, procurement, construction, interconnection, commissioning -> /", "10+ years commercial & industrial project experience -> /", "99.89% operational uptime -> /", "Serves manufacturing, agricultural, municipal, institutional, commercial facilities -> /", "Project example: Subaru of Indiana Automotive -> /", "Ranked #1 Commercial-Industrial Solar EPC in Indiana by Solar Power World -> /", "PE-engineered designs with performance modeling -> /", "Component procurement plan driven by warranty strength and supply-chain reliability -> /", "25-year production warranty and 5-year workmanship guarantee -> /", "Mission: provide best-in-class on-site solar power to manufacturing, agricultural, large energy load facilities -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Emergent Solar Energy is a commercial and industrial solar EPC contractor headquartered in the Purdue Research Park in West Lafayette, Indiana.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/emergentsolarenergy/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='emergent-solar-energy' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Emmaus Foods LLC operates its manufacturing facility and corporate office in Albertville, Alabama, in the heart of the poultry industry. The privately held limited liability company employs approximately 500 team members. While the food-focused business does not state a founding year, the company''s steel fabrication lineage traces to the April 1989 incorporation of Steel and Fabrication Industry, organized by veterans with sixty years of combined experience in steel fabrication, machining, and design.

The company serves two distinct lines: custom food manufacturing for national chain, food service, and hospitality customers, and heavy steel fabrication. The fabrication shop produces custom industrial tanks (including stainless steel), structural steel for commercial and industrial buildings and bridges, stainless steel ducting for semiconductor facilities, stacks for emissions compliance, pressure vessels, cyclones, scrubbers, fan housings, ductwork, hoppers, dampers, slide gates, filter housings, conveyors, and dewatering screen cabinets. It also offers industrial coating services. The operation is supported by a team of certified craftsmen, engineers, and designers.

Customers span the food industry — national chains, food service operators, and hospitality providers — as well as the semiconductor sector (for ducting), commercial and industrial construction (for structural steel and stacks), and a range of other industries that use coated or fabricated steel equipment.

