UPDATE companies SET description='Encore Renewable Energy is based in Burlington, Vermont. Founded as a brownfield redevelopment company, it has evolved into a full-service community-scale renewable energy project developer and operator. The company is a certified B Corporation and a portfolio company of SUSI Partners.

The firm develops, owns, and operates solar and energy storage projects, offering end-to-end services from concept through construction to long-term ownership. It specializes in reclaiming undervalued sites—landfills, brownfields, rooftops, and parking lots—and integrates dual-use approaches such as pollinator-friendly ground cover and solar grazing. Encore ranks as the #1 solar developer in Vermont and among the top 25 nationwide, with projects across the Northeast and a growing portfolio in Illinois.

Its customers include municipalities, businesses, institutions, utilities, non-profits, and landowners. Concrete examples include a 2.25‑megawatt landfill solar array for the Town of Derry, New Hampshire, projected to save $4 million over 25 years, and a multi‑project community solar portfolio under construction in Bureau, Henry, and Macoupin Counties, Illinois, which will maintain agricultural use through sheep grazing.

Encore’s differentiation rests on its B Corp certification, which embeds social and environmental performance into its legal structure, and its core values of integrity, determination, innovation, humility, curiosity, and impact. The company was started to turn brownfields into “brightfields,” leveraging clean energy to revitalize communities and address the climate crisis.', certifications=ARRAY['B Corp Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar project development", "Brownfield and landfill redevelopment", "Agrivoltaics (solar grazing, pollinator-friendly ground cover)", "Energy storage integration", "Community-scale solar project origination", "Project finance and ownership", "Construction management", "Long-term asset management", "Site assessment and permitting", "Grid interconnection"], "industries": ["Community solar", "Commercial solar", "Energy storage", "Brownfield redevelopment", "Agrivoltaics", "Renewable energy project development"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified B Corporation meeting verified social and environmental performance standards", "Ranked #1 solar developer in Vermont and top 25 in the U.S.", "Full-service model covering development, construction, and long-term ownership", "Specialized expertise in brownfield, landfill, and rooftop redevelopment", "Dual-use solutions including agrivoltaics (solar grazing) and pollinator habitats"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Burlington, VT -> db", "Certified B Corporation -> /, /about", "Portfolio company of SUSI Partners -> db (products)", "Full-service from concept to completion and long-term ownership -> /, /about, /services", "#1 Solar Developer in Vermont, Top 25 nationwide -> /, /about, /services", "Specializes in brownfield, landfill, rooftop redevelopment -> /, /services", "Dual-use solutions: pollinator-friendly ground cover, solar grazing -> /, /services", "Environmental impact numbers (auto miles offset, homes powered, barrels of oil replaced, etc.) -> /, /about", "Town of Derry, NH 2.25 MW landfill solar project -> /", "Illinois community solar portfolio in Bureau, Henry, Macoupin Counties -> /", "Core values: integrity, determination, innovation, humility, curiosity, impact -> /", "Mission: turning brownfields to brightfields -> /", "Customer types: municipalities, businesses, institutions, utilities, non-profits, landowners -> /, /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a full-service community-scale renewable energy project development and construction company", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/encore-renewable-energy/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='encore-renewable-energy' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company serves an installation territory that stretches from north of Green Bay through the Fox Valley and Madison area to the Wisconsin-Illinois border.

The firm provides full-service solar electrical products and services, specializing in residential and commercial photovoltaic installations. Its licensed and insured employees handle every step in-house — system design, permitting, installation, commissioning, inspection, and ongoing maintenance — without using subcontractors. To date, the team has installed more than 1,000 PV systems designed by owner Russel Endries.

Endries Solar & Electric works with homeowners and businesses across northern and southeastern Wisconsin. The company also assists customers with tax credits, incentives, and utility interconnection paperwork.

The company says its differentiators include NABCEP accreditation, membership on Wisconsin''s Focus on Energy Trade Ally list, and a commitment to using only its own trained installers. Russel Endries'' 20-plus years of electrical experience and the team''s combined 100-plus years in the trade are cited as the foundation for code-compliant, production-maximizing installations.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP (North American Board of Certified Energy Practitioners)','Wisconsin Focus on Energy Trade Ally']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Solar system design", "Solar system commissioning", "Solar system inspection", "Solar maintenance", "NABCEP certified installation", "Licensed and insured electrical work", "Solar incentive and tax credit consulting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Solar renewable energy"], "materials": ["Hanwha QCell solar modules", "Boviet bi-facial solar modules", "Enphase IQ microinverters", "Tesla Powerwall battery storage"], "equipment": ["Hanwha QCell modules", "Enphase IQ microinverters", "Tesla Powerwall backup batteries", "Boviet bi-facial modules"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All installation and maintenance performed by licensed, insured employees \u2014 no subcontractors", "NABCEP-accredited company (North American Board of Certified Energy Practitioners)", "Listed on Wisconsin Focus on Energy''s Trade Ally roster", "Over 1,000 PV systems installed, each designed by owner Russel Endries"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Oostburg, Wisconsin -> db", "Installation territory: north of Green Bay, Fox Valley, Madison, WI/IL border -> db", "Owner: Russel Endries, NABCEP-certified master electrician, first solar install 2008 -> /about", "Company provides full-service solar electrical products and services, specializes in residential and commercial PV installations -> /about", "All services performed by licensed and insured employees, no subcontractors -> /about, /", "Over 1,000 PV systems installed, designed by Russel Endries -> /about", "Serves residential and commercial customers in northern and southeastern Wisconsin -> /about", "Assists with tax credits, incentives, utility interconnection -> /", "NABCEP accredited, Wisconsin Focus on Energy Trade Ally -> /about", "Team combined 100+ years experience -> /about", "Specific equipment brands: Hanwha QCell, Enphase IQ, Tesla Powerwall, Boviet bi-facial -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Endries Solar & Electric is a full-service solar electrical product and service provider. With over 100 years of combined experience, we specialize in residential and commercial solar installations.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='endries-solar-and-electric' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Energy Technologies, Inc. (ETI) operates from Mansfield, Ohio, where it designs and builds rugged power electronics for demanding environments. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

ETI manufactures a broad range of high-reliability power equipment including uninterruptible power supplies (UPS), DC/AC inverters, frequency converters, power conditioners, power distribution units (PDUs), solar power systems, battery backup modules, engine generators, and rugged computers. Products are offered in rackmount, NEMA-rated, portable, and custom configurations. The company emphasizes that its designs originate as rugged rather than being adapted from commercial off-the-shelf units, and it validates hardware against military standards such as MIL-STD-167-1 and MIL-STD-810.

The company serves defense, industrial, telecommunications, and medical sectors. Its product families — Rugged Power™, Military Power®, Tactical Power®, Airborne Power®, Industrial Power Source®, and Extreme Power Source™ — address applications from fixed-site data centers to mobile tactical shelters, microgrids, and airborne platforms. Customers include military programs, telecom infrastructure operators, and industrial facilities requiring hardened power conditioning.

ETI states its differentiation lies in ground-up rugged design, full Mil-Spec compliance across product lines, and integrated solutions such as combined UPS/PDU chassis that reduce rack space and cabling. The firm also develops deployable tactical power plants, solar and wind generation kits, and environmental control units for field use.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL SPEC','MIL-STD-167-1','MIL-STD-810']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Uninterruptible Power Supply (UPS) manufacturing", "DC/AC inverter manufacturing", "Frequency converter manufacturing", "Power conditioner manufacturing", "Power distribution unit (PDU) manufacturing", "Solar power system manufacturing", "Battery backup system manufacturing", "Engine generator and power plant manufacturing", "Rugged computer and peripheral manufacturing", "Custom power system design", "Military specification (Mil-Spec) compliance testing", "Environmental testing (MIL-STD-167-1, MIL-STD-810)", "NEMA/IP rated enclosure manufacturing", "Tactical deployable power system integration", "Microgrid power management system manufacturing"], "industries": ["Defense / Military", "Industrial", "Telecommunications", "Medical", "Aerospace / Airborne"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Products designed rugged from the ground up, not ruggedized COTS", "Validated to MIL-STD-167-1 and MIL-STD-810", "Full Mil-Spec compliance across Military Power\u00ae line", "Integrated UPS/PDU chassis saving rack space and cabling", "Deployable tactical power, solar, wind, and microgrid solutions"], "facts_used": ["Mansfield, Ohio headquarters -> db", "Manufactures rugged UPS, inverters, frequency converters, power conditioners, PDUs, solar, battery backup, power generation, computer products -> /", "Serves defense, industrial, telecommunications, medical sectors -> /", "MIL SPEC certification -> db", "Products tested to MIL-STD-167-1 and MIL-STD-810 -> /", "Product lines: Rugged Power\u2122, Military Power\u00ae, Tactical Power\u00ae, Airborne Power\u00ae, Industrial Power Source\u00ae, Extreme Power Source\u2122 -> /", "Offers rackmount, NEMA, portable, custom configurations -> /", "LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/company/energy-technologies-inc./ -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Energy Technologies, Inc. (ETI) power site covering rugged, high-reliability global UPS, Power Inverters, Solar Power, Battery Backup, Power Conditioning, Frequency Conversion, Power Distribution, Power Generation and Computer products", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/energy-technologies-inc./"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='energy-technologies-inc-manufacturing-building' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Engineered Textile Products (ETP) is a family-owned textile fabrication company based in Mobile, Alabama. Founded in 1877, the business has been passed through five generations of the same family, growing from a local operation into a supplier of custom fabric solutions for clients across the United States and overseas.

The company specializes in custom-designed textile products for environmental containment, industrial protection, and recreational shading. Its product lines include ETP Environmental for site-specific liners and curtains, ETP Industrial for tarps and asset covers, ETP Artcraft Awnings for commercial and residential shade structures, ETP Sports for track-and-field surfaces and gym equipment, and ETP Racemarks for course marking and branding at regattas and triathlons. All items are fabricated to order using premium materials selected for durability in harsh conditions.

ETP serves the water management, agriculture, and manufacturing sectors, along with government agencies such as NASA, educational institutions, and event organizers worldwide. Past projects range from containment systems at the Port of Mobile to shade structures for high school athletic facilities and branding for international triathlon competitions.

The company attributes its longevity to a proactive approach: collaborating closely with customers to engineer precision-fit solutions that address specific environmental challenges, backed by 149 years of accumulated expertise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom textile fabrication", "Environmental containment liner fabrication", "Industrial tarp and curtain manufacturing", "Commercial and residential awning fabrication", "Sports facility surfacing and equipment fabrication", "Water event course marking and branding", "Sales and service"], "industries": ["Water management", "Agriculture", "Manufacturing", "Environmental protection", "Industrial facilities", "Recreation and sports", "Aquatic events", "Government", "Education"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom fabrication to exact customer specifications", "Five generations of family ownership since 1877", "Nationwide distribution and global export capability", "Site-specific environmental containment liners and curtains", "Champion-grade sports surfacing and water-event marking systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1877, family-owned, five generations -> /", "Headquartered in Mobile, Alabama -> db", "Custom fabrication of environmental and industrial fabric products -> db", "Nationwide distribution and global export -> db", "Product lines: ETP Environmental, Industrial, Artcraft Awnings, Sports, Racemarks -> /", "Industries served: water, agriculture, manufacturing, NASA, high schools, global events -> /", "Custom-designed textile solutions, premium materials, precision performance -> /", "Sales and service capability -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom fabrication of a large variety of environmental and industrial fabric products", "founded_year": "1877", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "soci