UPDATE companies SET description='Era Wire Inc. was founded in 1988 by Richard T. Rae in West Haven, Connecticut, initially operating as a wire straightening and cutting service and a dealer of used wire machinery. After Rae’s passing in 2015, his son Rich Jr. assumed leadership, adding an on-site distribution warehouse and through-feed centerless grinding to create a one-stop shop for ferrous and non-ferrous wire needs.

The company specializes in precision wire straightening and cutting for round, flat, and shaped materials across all tempers and alloys, complemented by heat treating, torsion straightening, and wire forming. Its through-feed centerless grinding service provides an alternative to turning and milling for components requiring tight diameter and surface-finish tolerances. The Quick Wire Program stocks pre-cut 304 spring-tempered stainless steel (including 304V and 316LVM), aluminum, copper, titanium, and high/low carbon steels, offering same-day shipping on stocked items.

Primary markets include the medical device industry, where ERA Wire supplies precision-straightened Bright Diamond Drawn wire for Swiss screw machining, and broader industrial sectors requiring ferrous and non-ferrous wire processing.

Founded on a “customer first” philosophy summarized by the tagline “We give it to you straight,” ERA Wire maintains ISO 9001:2015 certification (since 2004) and adheres to RoHS III, REACH Annex XVII, California Proposition 65, and conflict-minerals (3TG) regulations, ensuring traceable quality and regulatory compliance for every shipment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS III compliance','REACH Annex XVII compliance','California Proposition 65 compliance','ISPM-15/IPPC (PRL) certified','Conflict Minerals (3TG) compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision wire straightening and cutting", "Through-feed centerless grinding", "Heat treating", "Torsion straightening", "Wire forming", "Quick wire program (same-day shipping of pre-cut wire)", "Wire machinery sales (used equipment)", "Parts and tooling supply"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Swiss screw machining", "General industrial wire processing"], "materials": ["Ferrous metals", "Non-ferrous metals", "Stainless steel (304, 304V, 316LVM)", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Titanium", "High carbon steel", "Low carbon steel", "Bright Diamond Drawn wire"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for stocked pre-cut wire", "tolerances": "Close/precision tolerances", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on stocked pre-cut wire via Quick Wire Program", "Through-feed centerless grinding as a cost-effective alternative to turning/milling", "ISO 9001:2015 certified since 2004", "Full compliance with RoHS III, REACH Annex XVII, California Prop 65, and 3TG conflict-minerals rules", "One-stop shop for ferrous and non-ferrous wire: straightening, cutting, grinding, and stock"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 by Richard T. Rae -> /", "Relocated to West Haven, CT in 1995 -> /", "Son Rich Jr. took over in 2015, added distribution warehouse and centerless grinding -> /", "Services: wire straightening/cutting, centerless grinding, heat treating, torsion straightening, wire forming -> /", "Quick Wire Program: same-day shipping of pre-cut wire (304, 304V, 316LVM, aluminum, copper, titanium, carbon steels) -> /", "Medical industry focus: precision medical wire, Bright Diamond Drawn materials, Swiss screw machine customers -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified since 2004 -> /quality", "Compliance: RoHS III, REACH Annex XVII, California Prop 65, Conflict Minerals (3TG), ISPM-15/IPPC -> /quality", "Materials: ferrous, non-ferrous, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, titanium, carbon steels -> /", "Tagline: ''We give it to you straight'' -> /", "Address: 19-25 Locust Street, West Haven, CT 06516 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "ERA Wire Inc., founded in 1988 by Richard T. Rae, began as a wire straightening and cutting service and used wire machinery dealer.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ISPM-15/IPPC certified for international wood packaging"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='era-wire-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Erhardt Woodworks operates a woodworking workshop in Bismarck, North Dakota, serving residential and commercial clients across Burleigh and Morton Counties. The company handcrafts every piece in its Bismarck facility and tailors each project to the client''s home, business, or remodeling needs.

The shop produces custom European-style cabinets, painted cabinets, MDF doors and drawer fronts, Baltic birch dovetail drawer boxes, epoxy resin tables, live-edge furniture, and live-edge countertops. Its capabilities cover design, fabrication, finishing, delivery, and installation. Materials include solid hardwoods, MDF, high-quality veneers, Baltic birch, and premium epoxy resin systems formulated to resist yellowing, heat, and moisture. Typical turnaround ranges from four to six weeks for smaller builds such as vanity cabinets, and eight to twelve weeks for full kitchen projects.

Erhardt Woodworks serves homeowners, general contractors, and business owners in Bismarck, Mandan, Lincoln, and surrounding communities, with select work extending across North Dakota. Projects range from single live-edge tables and accent cabinets to complete kitchen renovations and commercial fit-outs.

The company differentiates itself through color- and profile-matching services that replicate existing door styles using MDF or solid wood, a showroom where clients can examine finishes in person, and a commitment to managing each project from initial design through final installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry (European style)", "Painted cabinets", "MDF doors and drawer fronts", "Baltic birch dovetail drawer boxes", "Epoxy resin tables", "Live-edge furniture", "Live-edge countertops", "Design services", "Fabrication", "Finishing (stain, paint, epoxy)", "Delivery", "Installation", "Color matching", "Profile matching", "Showroom consultation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Remodeling/Construction"], "materials": ["Solid hardwoods", "MDF (medium-density fiberboard)", "High-quality veneers", "Baltic birch", "Epoxy resin"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Smaller custom builds (vanity or accent cabinets): 4\u20136 weeks; full kitchen projects: 8\u201312 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted in Bismarck workshop", "Full-service from design to installation", "Color- and profile-matching for existing cabinetry", "Premium epoxy resin systems resistant to yellowing, heat, and moisture", "Professional delivery and installation within Bismarck and surrounding areas"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bismarck, North Dakota -> /", "Services: custom cabinets, painted cabinets, MDF doors, epoxy resin tables, live-edge furniture, live edge countertops, Baltic birch dovetail drawer boxes -> /", "Materials: solid hardwoods, MDF, high-quality veneers, Baltic birch, epoxy resin -> /", "Turnaround times: 4-6 weeks for smaller builds, 8-12 weeks for full kitchen -> /", "Service area: Bismarck, Mandan, Lincoln, Burleigh and Morton Counties, select North Dakota -> /", "Showroom in Bismarck -> /", "Design to installation process -> /", "Color and profile matching -> /", "Premium epoxy res