UPDATE companies SET description='Evotronics Inc is a family-owned PCB contract manufacturing company based in Minneapolis, Minnesota. Founded in 1995 by Tam Tran, the business is now led by co-owners Anh Tran and Ken Nguyen. The company began as a provider of design, manufacture, test, distribution, and repair services for electronic assemblies serving original equipment manufacturers.

The shop offers a full range of electronics assembly services, including through-hole and surface-mount assembly, custom cable assembly, electro-mechanical assembly, and final box-build with labeling and serialization. Capabilities extend to engineering support, first-article test runs, rework, and conformal coating application. The facility is climate-controlled and monitored by a surveillance system, and the company states it handles both small prototype runs and higher-volume production.

Evotronics serves OEMs across retail, consumer, industrial, medical, and defense/aerospace sectors. Customers rely on the company for prototyping, design-for-manufacturing feedback, and BOM alternative component sourcing.

The company emphasizes a no-stencil solder paste process for rapid prototyping, automated axial insertion for ammo-pack and cut-tape components, and an in-house flood box for in-line washing. Its quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015, with UL and FDA registrations, and it maintains an ESD-safe environment audited by a third party.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL Certified','FDA Registered','EDS Safe Environment (Audited by Third Party)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB prototyping", "First article test runs", "Through-hole assembly", "Surface mount assembly", "Custom cable assembly", "Rework and repair services", "Engineering services to customer design", "Hand placement for odd-shaped components", "Flood box in-line wash", "Adhesive application (UV, epoxy, conformal coating)", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Final box-build assembly (labeling, serialization, decals)", "Engineering modifications post-completion", "Automated through-hole axial insertion", "BOM alternative component assistance", "Design for manufacturing (DFM)", "No-stencil solder paste printing", "KIC thermal profiling", "Wire soldering on PCB", "Repair and return services"], "industries": ["Retail", "Consumer", "Industrial", "Medical", "Defense and aerospace"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automated Axial Machine", "KIC Profiler", "Flood Box", "Brady Label Maker", "Semi-Automatic Axial and Radial Prep Machines", "RF Enclosure Room"], "volume": "Small production runs to higher volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No-stencil solder paste printing for rapid prototypes", "Automated axial insertion for ammo-pack and cut-tape components", "In-house flood box for in-line washing", "Full box-build assembly including labeling and serialization", "ISO 9001:2015, UL, and FDA registered quality system"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1995 by Tam Tran -> /about", "Family-owned, co-owners Anh Tran and Ken Nguyen -> /about", "Location Minneapolis, Minnesota -