UPDATE companies SET description='Experienced Solar is based in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company was founded in 2015 by Kevin Goodreau, who brought 16 years of experience from his previous venture, Direct Power & Water Corporation (DPW), started in 1993. Goodreau served as CEO until 2022, when his son-in-law Mike Rogers acquired the business. A core team of professionals from DPW continues to operate under the Experienced Solar name.

As a licensed electrical contractor (EE98 #390475) and a NABCEP-certified PV installer, Experienced Solar engineers, designs, and installs grid-tied and remote solar electric systems for residential, commercial, and industrial clients. The firm also supplies and installs Generac generators and PWRcell energy storage systems. Every project is handled turnkey, from initial site survey and electrical load analysis through custom system engineering, permitting, installation, and commissioning. The company emphasizes precise array tilt and azimuth calculations to maximize energy production, and reports having completed hundreds of grid-tied installations with a sub‑1% issue rate over a decade.

The customer base spans Albuquerque and a wide surrounding region including Santa Fe, Rio Rancho, Los Lunas, and numerous pueblos and counties across central New Mexico. Commercial clients range from small businesses to large-scale real estate developments, with the company highlighting solar carport structures that provide both shade and power generation. Residential and remote off‑grid installations round out the portfolio.

Experienced Solar differentiates itself through a rigorous site‑survey process that evaluates feeder cables, transformer capacity, panel bus‑bar ampacity, and roof or ground conditions before any proposal. The firm promotes direct, ongoing customer access before, during, and after installation, and targets commercial payback periods of three to five years by leveraging federal tax credits, MACRS depreciation, and state gross‑receipts‑tax exemptions.', certifications=ARRAY['North American Board of Certified Energy Practitioners (NABCEP) Certified PV Installer','Licensed Electrical Contractor (EE98 #390475)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system engineering and design", "Grid-tied solar installation", "Remote/off-grid solar installation", "Electrical contracting (EE98 #390475)", "NABCEP-certified PV installation", "Site survey and electrical load analysis", "Custom array tilt and azimuth calculation", "Solar carport design and installation", "Generac generator installation", "PWRcell energy storage installation", "Turnkey project management", "Permitting and commissioning", "Commercial solar financial analysis (tax credits, MACRS)"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Commercial real estate"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turnkey project management from site survey through commissioning", "NABCEP\u2011certified PV installation and licensed electrical contracting", "Custom array tilt and azimuth engineering for maximum production", "Direct customer access throughout the project lifecycle", "Commercial payback periods of 3\u20135 years via tax incentives and depreciation"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2015 by Kevin Goodreau -> /about", "Sold to Mike Rogers in 2022 -> /about", "Licensed electrical contractor EE98 #390475 -> /", "NABCEP Certified PV installer -> /", "Serves residential, commercial, industrial customers -> /", "Offers Generac generators and PWRcell clean energy -> /", "Turnkey solar system design and installation -> /", "Commercial solar carports -> /services", "Payback periods 3-5 years for commercial -> /services", "Free consultation includes electric bill analysis -> /services", "Headquartered in Albuquerque, NM -> db", "More than 20 years of expertise (Goodreau) -> /", "Hundreds of grid-tied systems with <1% problems -> /", "Core team from DPW -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Experienced Solar is a licensed electrical contractor, specializing in bringing residential, commercial and industrial customers the many benefits of tailored solar systems.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='experienced-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Exponent Assembly operates from Carrollton, Texas, where it was founded in 1996 as a contract manufacturing business. The company has built a reputation for customer service and quality over nearly three decades.

The shop specializes in printed circuit board assembly, offering surface-mount, through-hole, and mixed-technology processes with pick-and-place equipment rated at 30,000 parts per hour. It handles prototyping through medium-to-large volume runs (hundreds to thousands of boards), and provides electromechanical assembly including wire harnesses, cable assemblies, and box builds. Additional capabilities include selective and wave soldering, automated optical inspection (2D/3D), 3D solder paste inspection, test development, rework, and repair. The facility also supports consignment, turnkey, and semi-turnkey procurement models.

Exponent serves customers in automotive, audio-visual, surveillance and optics, defense, computer and electronics, and industrial equipment sectors. Clients range from companies needing quick-turn prototypes to those requiring full turnkey production with inventory management and traceability.

