UPDATE companies SET description='F&P America Manufacturing Inc. operates in Troy, Ohio, where it was founded in 1993 as a distribution and assembly facility for its Japanese parent company, F-Tech. F-Tech traces its roots to 1947 in Saitama Prefecture, Japan, where it began as a metal toy manufacturer. In 1959 the company started supplying motorcycle parts to Honda Motor Co., Ltd., later becoming a tier-one automotive supplier. To support Honda’s North American production, F-Tech opened a Canadian plant in 1986 and established the Ohio operation as demand grew.

The company produces pedal assemblies, suspension components, front and rear subframes, and clutch pedals with integrated sensor assemblies. Manufacturing processes include progressive and traditional stamping of rolled steel, traditional and innovative welding, hydroforming of steel tube, painting, and final assembly of sub-assemblies. The Troy facility employs roughly 900 associates and has doubled its building footprint twice, in 1996 and 2001. F&P America is part of a global network of 19 locations under the F-Tech family.

F&P America serves the automotive industry as a tier-one supplier. Its customer base includes Honda, Toyota, and General Motors, providing bolt-in parts ready for direct installation on assembly lines.

The company emphasizes a commitment to excellence through continuous improvement of technology, processes, facilities, and capabilities. It attributes its quality standards to a quality-minded workforce operating in a safe, clean, state-of-the-art environment.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF-16949','ISO 14001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Research & Development", "Progressive stamping", "Traditional stamping", "Welding", "Hydroforming", "Painting", "Assembly"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": ["Rolled steel", "Steel tube"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["19 global locations under the F-Tech family", "IATF-16949 and ISO 14001 certified", "In-house R&D through F.tech R&D North America", "Hydroforming of steel tube for complex automotive parts", "Painted and assembled sub-assemblies ready for installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1993 in Troy, Ohio -> /about", "Parent company F-Tech established 1947 in Saitama Prefecture, Japan -> /about", "Relationship with Honda began 1959 -> /about", "F-Tech expanded to North America 1986 with Canadian plant -> /about", "Initially distribution and assembly facility -> /about", "Mass production for Honda started 1994, added Welding and Painting -> /about", "Doubled building capacity 1996 and 2001, added Stamping and Hydroforming -> /about", "Approximately 900 employees -> /about", "Customers: Honda, Toyota, General Motors -> /about", "Certifications: IATF-16949 and ISO 14001 -> /about", "Capabilities: R&D, Stamping, Welding, Hydroforming, Painting, Assembly -> /capabilities", "Products: pedal assemblies, subframes, suspension parts, clutch pedals with sensors -> /", "19 global locations -> /", "Headquarters: Troy, Ohio -> db", "Company type: Manufacturer -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "F&P America Mfg., Inc. is a world class, Tier-one, international automotive systems supplier located in Troy, Ohio.", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "approximately 900", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='f-p-america-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='F.A.T.S. Parts, operating under the name Foreign Auto & Truck Supply, has served the Anchorage, Alaska area from its two locations on East International Airport Road. The business supplies automotive parts and operates a full-service repair shop, though the founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company stocks a wide range of replacement parts for virtually any make and model, backed by a 12-month or 12,000-mile warranty on both parts and labor. Its service department performs tune‑ups, fuel‑injection service, front‑end alignments, tire work, pre‑purchase inspections, electrical diagnosis, brake repair, and scheduled maintenance. The shop also holds I/M certification for emissions testing and repair.

The staff assists with part selection using VIN, year, make, model, and engine data, and the company emphasizes factory‑tested components that are inspected before sale.

