-a-t-s-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The FARM (Food, Agriculture, Research, Manufacturing Center) accelerator sits on the Muskegon Community College campus in Muskegon, Michigan. Launched by the West Michigan Food Processing Association (WMFPA) with the Community Foundation for Muskegon County and Muskegon Community College—and affiliated with Michigan State University’s food-processing programs—the project secured a $2 million state infrastructure grant in 2019. Construction started in June 2020 and finished in early 2021. The center was built to help stage-one and stage-two food entrepreneurs, plus established companies needing offsite test-manufacturing space.

The facility offers 8,000 square feet of flexible, food-grade suites for commercial fruit and vegetable processing. It meets USDA and FDA standards and includes loading docks, refrigeration and freezer storage, energy-efficient systems, and waste and water handling. Tenants bring their own processing equipment and lease space on flexible terms, graduating to their own plants as they grow. The site also houses the MSU Mobile Processing Lab, a trailer-scale unit used for teaching and career outreach.

FARM serves early-stage food-processing ventures and mature firms seeking pilot-scale production, connecting them with venture capital, student talent from MSU and MCC, and regional kitchen incubators like Kitchen 242 and the Starting Block. Target industries include food processing and agriculture, with a focus on companies planning North American or export expansion. The center also supports workforce development through MSU’s certificate and degree programs. WMFPA designed FARM as a one-stop shop to move innovations from concept to commercialization, strengthen job training, and bolster West Michigan’s food-processing cluster.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food-grade facility leasing", "Incubation and acceleration services", "Product development support", "Access to MSU Mobile Processing Lab", "Workforce training collaboration", "Venture capital connection"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Agriculture", "Food manufacturing", "Education and workforce development"], "materials": ["Fruits", "Vegetables"], "equipment": ["MSU Mobile Processing Lab"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Food-grade industrial suites with flexible lease terms", "8,000 sq ft USDA/FDA-compliant manufacturing space", "On-site MSU Mobile Processing Lab for training and demonstration", "Located on Muskegon Community College campus with MSU affiliation", "Access to venture capital and regional incubator network"], "facts_used": ["Location: Muskegon, Michigan on Muskegon Community College campus -> /", "Facility: 8,000 sq ft food-grade manufacturing space for fruit/vegetable processing -> /", "Compliance: USDA and FDA requirements -> /", "Features: loading docks, refrigeration/freezers, waste/water handling -> /", "Affiliation: Muskegon Community College and Michigan State University -> /", "Construction: began June 2020, completed early 2021 -> /", "Purpose: accelerator for food processing startups/companies -> /", "Management: Clarence Rudat as MSU/FARM Manager -> /", "Funding: $2M+ state infrastructure grant awarded 2019 -> /", "Tenants furnish own equipment -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "FARM (Food, Agriculture, Research, Manufacturing Center) accelerator and business development center targeted at stage one or two entrepreneurial companies or existing mature ones that are looking for an offsite location for test manufacturing of new products.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/81299091/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='farm-food-processing-accelerator' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='FCPS Electric is based in Bryant, Arkansas, and was founded in 1977 by Lorin Fleming. The company remains independently owned and operated from its original location, having grown from a one‑man operation into a full team of factory‑trained, certified technicians serving the entire state and holding licenses in Tennessee, Texas, Alabama, Iowa, Louisiana, and Mississippi.

The firm provides full‑service electrical contracting for industrial and commercial facilities. Its scope covers electrical design‑build, medium‑ and high‑voltage switchgear installation and service, standby and prime‑power generator installation and maintenance, custom power‑distribution panel design and fabrication, power and control cable wiring, petroleum‑industry electrical work for convenience stores, scheduled equipment inspections, emergency troubleshooting, and 24/7 emergency response. Additional capabilities include aerial lift services using bucket trucks, network cabling and security integration (as an authorized integrator for Turing, Axis, and Brivo), automation and controls, and testing and consulting.

FCPS serves a range of sectors including healthcare (University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences), metal processing (Ryerson), water treatment (Conway County Regional Water), and petroleum retail. Its customer base spans industrial plants, commercial buildings, and critical‑infrastructure operators throughout Arkansas and neighboring states.

The company emphasizes factory‑certified expertise, a live‑answer 24/7 phone policy, and long‑term client relationships — some spanning 20‑plus years. Independent ownership allows it to set its own service standards, and a safety‑first culture is cited as non‑negotiable. Being Arkansas‑based, not a national chain, is presented as a deliberate choice to keep accountability local.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical design\u2011build", "Switchgear installation & service (medium/high voltage)", "Generator installation & maintenance (standby/prime power)", "Custom power\u2011distribution panel design, fabrication & installation", "Cable & wire installation (power and control)", "Petroleum industry electrical (fuel systems, convenience stores)", "Scheduled equipment inspections", "Equipment failure troubleshooting", "24/7 emergency electrical service", "Aerial lift services (bucket trucks, aerial platforms)", "Network cabling", "Network security integration (Turing, Axis, Brivo)", "Automation & controls", "Testing & consulting", "Component sourcing & procurement", "Panel wiring & assembly", "Maintenance contracts with priority scheduling"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Metal processing", "Water treatment", "Petroleum / convenience stores", "Industrial facilities", "Commercial facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Bucket trucks", "Aerial platforms"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Factory\u2011certified technicians on every project", "Live 24/7 phone answer \u2014 no voicemail for emergencies", "Client relationships exceeding 20 years", "Independent ownership enabling direct service decisions", "Safety\u2011first protocols with no shortcuts"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Bryant, AR -> db", "Founded 1977 by Lorin Fleming -> /about-us", "Independently owned -> /about-us", "Licensed in TN, TX, AL, IA, LA, MS, AR -> /", "Services: design-build, switchgear, generators, panels, wiring, petroleum, in