UPDATE companies SET description='Fabricated Steel Products (FSP) was founded by Warren Tabor in 1986 in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. The family-owned business began as a steel fabrication shop serving the Gulf Coast region and has since expanded its reach nationally and internationally.

Operating from two shops in Baton Rouge, FSP is an AISC-certified fabricator providing structural and miscellaneous steel fabrication, steel detailing, and engineered connection design. The company employs 75 people and produces 600–900 tons of steel per month. Its equipment includes a fully automated Voortman beam line, CNC plasma tables, drill lines, punch lines, and forming equipment. In-house detailing uses SDS/2 and Tekla for BIM project services and clash detection, while barcode tracking follows every piece through fabrication. Additional services cover galvanizing, plate forming, structural coating, sandblasting, and painting.

FSP supplies structural steel to the oil, gas, petrochemical, power, paper and pulp, food processing, automotive, municipal, and defense industries. Customers range from large industrial projects to smaller orders across the Gulf Coast and worldwide.

The company emphasizes being large enough for any job yet small enough to align with partners, focusing on continuous improvement, safety, and family values. Its mission centers on superior products, service, and on-time delivery to build long-term partnerships.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Structural Steel Building Fabricator Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Miscellaneous steel fabrication", "Steel detailing", "Engineered connection design", "Galvanizing", "Plate forming", "Structural coating", "Sandblasting", "Painting", "Custom fabrication", "CNC plasma cutting", "CNC drilling", "CNC punching", "Layout", "Forming", "BIM services", "Clash detection", "Barcode tracking", "Voortman beam line operation", "Flux-cored arc welding (FCAW)"], "industries": ["Oil", "Gas", "Petrochemical", "Power", "Paper & pulp", "Food processing", "Automotive", "Municipal", "Defense"], "materials": ["Structural steel", "Zinc (for galvanizing)"], "equipment": ["Voortman beam line with layout", "CNC plasma tables", "CNC drill lines", "CNC punch lines", "Layout equipment", "Forming equipment", "SDS/2 software", "Tekla software"], "volume": "600-900 tons per month", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AISC-certified structural steel building fabricator", "Two Baton Rouge shops with 600\u2013900 tons monthly capacity", "In-house detailing and connection design via SDS/2 and Tekla for BIM", "Barcode tracking of every piece through fabrication", "Fully automated Voortman beam line with CNC plasma, drill, and punch lines"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Warren Tabor in 1986 -> /about-us", "Family-owned business -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Baton Rouge, Louisiana -> /", "Two shops in Baton Rouge -> /", "AISC certified fabricator -> /", "75 employees -> /about-us", "Volume 600-900 tons per month -> /", "Equipment: Voortman beam line, CNC plasma tables, drill lines, punch lines, layout, forming equipment -> /", "In-house detailing with