UPDATE companies SET description='Falcon Engineering Corporation operates from Mesa, Arizona, as a women-owned small business specializing in mission-critical tactical textiles and parachutes. The company emphasizes safety-critical soft goods for commercial and military aviation, though its founding year and founders are not publicly disclosed.

The firm provides engineering, prototyping, cut-and-sew production, and inspection under a single AS9100 Rev D and ISO 9001:2015 quality system. Its product line includes whole-airframe recovery parachutes for Cirrus SR20, SR22, and SF50 Vision Jet aircraft; T-11 and MC-6 personnel parachutes; LCLV, G-12, and 26-foot cargo parachutes with multi-line loop lines; and deceleration parachutes for platforms such as the B-52. Additional output covers slings, tie-downs, tactical gear, inflatables, and strap assemblies, supported by CNC machining and fabrication capabilities. The company reports more than 10,000 parachutes shipped and holds 38 National Stock Numbers under Federal Supply Class 1670.

Customers span commercial aviation (notably Cirrus Aircraft) and military sectors including airborne personnel operations, aerial resupply, and aircraft deceleration. The Forestry Service (specification 5100-86) is also listed among served markets.

Falcon positions itself on delivering safety-critical soft goods that must function correctly the first time, integrating design, 3D modeling, first-article build, and volume production within one certified quality system, citing a 99 percent on-time delivery rate.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100 Rev D','ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering design of deceleration and recovery systems", "3D and 2D modeling", "First article prototyping", "Cut-and-sew manufacturing", "Quality inspection and control", "Production lot manufacturing", "CNC machining", "Metal fabrication", "Textile cutting and sewing", "Sling and tie-down assembly", "Parachute canopy and harness assembly", "Tactical gear fabrication", "Strap assembly", "Inflatable fabrication", "Forestry service equipment (5100-86)"], "industries": ["Commercial aviation", "Military aviation", "Military personnel/airborne operations", "Military cargo and aerial delivery", "Military aircraft deceleration", "Forestry service"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to production volumes; 10,000+ parachutes shipped", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AS9100 Rev D and ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "Women-Owned Small Business designation", "38 parachute NSNs under FSC 1670", "Engineering, prototyping, cut-and-sew, and inspection in-house", "99% on-time delivery rate"], "facts_used": ["Mesa, Arizona headquarters -> db", "Women-Owned Small Business -> /", "AS9100 Rev D certified -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "12 Years in business -> /", "10,000+ parachutes shipped -> /", "99% on-time delivery -> /", "38 parachute NSNs \u00b7 FSC 1670 -> /", "Engineering, cut-and-sew production and inspection under one roof -> /", "Commercial aircraft recovery parachutes for Cirrus SR20, SR22, SF50 -> /", "Military personnel parachutes T-11 and MC-6 -> /", "Military cargo parachutes LCLV, G-12, 26 ft and loop lines -> /", "Military deceleration parachutes for B-52 -> /",