UPDATE companies SET description='Ferric, Inc. is a semiconductor company headquartered in New York, New York, founded in 2021. The company pioneers integrated voltage regulators (IVRs) for next-generation computing, leveraging proprietary thin-film magnetic materials and CMOS-integrated ferromagnetic power inductor technology.

Ferric designs and manufactures a family of IVR products including the Fe1728 flexible multi-output converter, the Fe1736 16-phase buck converter, the Fe1766 ultra-high current density IVR, and the Fe1767 Newport dual-sided IVR. The Fe1766 delivers 160 A in an 8×4.4 mm² package with 4.5 A/mm² current density and 93% conversion efficiency, while the Fe1767 Newport provides 145 A TDC in an 8.9×5.6 mm², 1.2 mm thick package. The company holds over 40 patents stemming from a decade of research and claims its solutions are more than 10× smaller than conventional discrete approaches.

Ferric targets AI and data center operators, high-performance computing clusters, and mobile and consumer electronics manufacturers. Its technology has been proven in Apple products since 2021, and the company emphasizes scalability for hyperscaler environments. Integration options include back-side PCB attach, land-side package attach, dual-side attach, substrate embedding, die-side attach, and PCB embedding for vertical power delivery.

Ferric states its differentiation lies in the highest current density in the industry, elimination of bulky discrete components, and up to 74% component count reduction. The proprietary thin-film magnetic material breakthrough enables integrated power management with >10 MHz regulation bandwidth and 90–93% conversion efficiency, simplifying system design and improving power integrity.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Integrated Voltage Regulator (IVR) design and manufacturing", "Thin-film magnetic materials deposition", "CMOS-integrated ferromagnetic power inductor fabrication", "Vertical power delivery integration", "Back-side PCB attach", "Land-side package attach", "Dual-side attach", "Substrate embedded integration", "Die-side package attach", "PCB embedded integration", "Failure analysis", "Quality management (ISO 9001:2015)"], "industries": ["AI and Data Centers", "High-Performance Computing", "Mobile and Consumer Electronics", "Other Applications", "Hyperscaler environments"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary thin-film magnetic materials technology", "CMOS-integrated ferromagnetic power inductor technology", "Highest current density in the industry (4.5 A/mm\u00b2)", "Reduces component count by up to 74%", ">10\u00d7 smaller than conventional discrete solutions", "40+ patents built on a decade of research", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2021 -> db", "Headquartered in New York, NY -> db", "Semiconductor company pioneering IVRs -> /", "Proprietary thin-film magnetic materials technology -> /", "CMOS-integrated ferromagnetic power inductor technology -> /", "40+ patents built on a decade of research -> /", "Product lines: Fe1728, Fe1736, Fe1766, Fe1767 Newport -> /", "Fe1766 delivers 160A in 8x4.4mm, 4.5 A/mm\u00b2, 93% efficiency -> /", "Fe1767 Newport delivers 145A TDC in 8.9x5.6mm, 1.2mm thick -> /", "Fe1736 delivers 56A in 20mm\u00b2 -> /", "Fe1728 reduces component count by up to 74% -> /", "Industries: AI and Data Centers, High-Performance Computing, Mobile and Consumer Electronics -> /", "Proven in Apple products since 2021 -> /", "Integration options: back-side PCB attach, land-side package attach, dual-side attach, substrate embedded, die-side attach, PCB embedded -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "RoHS compliance -> /quality", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Ferric is a semiconductor company pioneering Integrated Voltage Regulators (IVRs) for the next generation of computing.", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ferric/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ferric-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business is led by Wayne Fiorenza, a third-generation master wood craftsman who learned the trade from his father, who in turn had been taught by his own father in Italy.

The shop produces custom furniture, architectural millwork, and cabinetry for both residential and executive office spaces. Its portfolio includes armoires, fireplace mantels, entertainment centers, computer desk systems, libraries, studies, kitchen cabinets, bathroom vanities, hidden doors, wall units, home theater cabinetry, and island wood countertops.

Completed installations are documented in cities including Irving, Plano, Argyle, Flower Mound, Dallas, Frisco, Southlake, and surrounding communities.

