UPDATE companies SET description='The company is now headquartered in Las Vegas, Nevada, and operates three manufacturing facilities across the United States and Canada. A 2020 investment from private equity firm Novacap supports its continued expansion.

The company designs, engineers, and manufactures commercial furniture in-house for high-use environments including student housing, hospitality, community living, government, staff housing, and maritime sectors. Its vertically integrated operation spans a 309,000-square-foot factory in Las Vegas, a 40,000-square-foot facility in Canada, and a newer Canadian plant producing laminate panels. With a workforce of over 630 people, Foliot has delivered furniture for more than 1.25 million rooms across North America.

Clients include universities such as Savannah College of Art and Design and Cornell University, hospitality brands like Hilton and LivSmart Studios, and organizations including WestCare, UNLV/Mojave Counseling, and Spacesaver Interiors. The firm''s portfolio covers large-scale projects for educational housing, government facilities, and community living developments.

Foliot emphasizes vertical integration to ensure quality control, cost efficiency, and streamlined operations from material sourcing to final installation. Since 2019, it has reduced recordable workplace injuries by nearly 80 percent, and in 2024 deployed 17 collaborative robots across its facilities. The company cites its mission to provide a harmonious environment for clients, employees, and the community as a founding principle.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial furniture design", "Furniture engineering", "Laminate furniture manufacturing", "Seating and upholstery production", "Vertical integration (in-house design, engineering, production)", "Project management and logistics", "Design advisory and personalization", "Quick-ship program", "Warranty and lifecycle support", "Sustainable manufacturing practices", "Collaborative robot (cobot) integration"], "industries": ["Student Housing", "Hospitality", "Community Living", "Government", "Staff Housing", "Maritime", "Educational Housing"], "materials": ["Laminate", "Upholstery fabrics"], "equipment": ["Collaborative robots (cobots)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1991 in Montreal by Daniel Foliot -> /about-us", "Headquarters Las Vegas, Nevada -> db", "3 manufacturing facilities in US and Canada -> /", "630+ person workforce -> db", "Over 1.25 million rooms delivered -> /", "Vertically integrated manufacturing -> /", "Industries: student housing, hospitality, community living, government, staff housing, maritime -> /", "Customer examples: Savannah College of Art and Design, Cornell University, Spacesaver Interiors, WestCare, UNLV/Mojave Counseling, Ovation -> /", "Novacap investment 2020 -> /about-us", "17 Cobots deployed 2024 -> /about-us", "Reduced workplace injuries 80% since 2019 -> db", "Laminate furniture and seating/upholstery production -> /about-us", "Design advisory, project oversight, logistics services -> /services", "Facility sizes: 309,000 sq ft Las Vegas, 40,000 sq ft Canada, 1,800 sq ft original Montreal -> /about-us", "Mission: harmonious environment for clients, employees, community -> /about-us", "Industry-leading warranties & lifecycle support -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract furniture manufacturer serving student housing, hospitality, community living, government, and beyond for 35 years.", "founded_year": "1991", "employee_count": "630+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='foliot-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Processing Equipment Company, LLC is based in Kalamazoo, Michigan. The limited liability company focuses on the food processing equipment sector.

The company buys, sells, and rebuilds used food processing equipment, ranging from individual machines such as slicers, conveyors, and peelers to complete processing lines and plants. It also provides a suite of services including brokerage, auction management, investment recovery, equipment appraisals, line layout design, installation, equipment financing, consulting, and leasing. In addition, the company supplies new cutting blades, notably Urschel blades, for mechanical cutting machines.

Its customer base spans the global food processing industry, serving sectors such as fresh vegetable and fruit processing, refrigeration, ice production, freezing, cannery operations, and packaging. The company’s inventory includes equipment for applications like apple cutting, bulk filling, dewatering, washing, optical sorting, drying, cheese shredding, and hydrocooling, among others.

